                <pb facs="0250" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received July 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan strongly recommends that the telegraph company accept the offer made by
                    the Chilean Government to pay the expenses of opening communication with
                    Valparaiso and to give guaranties against damages to cable.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
